<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY TALKS ORE MINE SALE WITH CHINESE-US FIRMS.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY TALKS ORE MINE SALE WITH CHINESE-US FIRMS.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's state privatisation agency APV began talks with a Chinese-U.S. consortium about the sale of a 90 percent stake in Recski Ore Mines Rt, APV said.</p>
<p>The consortium, made up of China Metallurgical Construction and New York-based Oil Capital, has won a privatisation tender for the stake, ahead of consortium of Austrian companies, APV officials told a news conference.</p>
<p>The winner's bid was slightly below the face value of the stake APV CEO Pal Szabo said.</p>
<p>The consortium undertook the pay the price, on which the talks has not been closed yet, and to develop the copper mine of Recski, investing further $138 million in Hungary.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
